Notebook[{
Cell["", "Package",ExpressionUUID->"19520a93-7923-48c4-99b6-5e54a5a53399"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gravitational-Electrostatic Equilibrium ", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990109258737499*^9, 3.990109285079598*^9}, 
   3.990109594450819*^9},ExpressionUUID->"47103a1f-8892-4be8-b1b5-\
b429b49f103c"],

Cell["Brian Beckman", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990109327549945*^9, 
  3.9901093424140377`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4dd3ed93-c60a-4357-9732-\
db053ac1d086"],

Cell["June 2026", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990109344636537*^9, 
  3.9901093471946*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"711d228a-cf26-4ffd-9a1a-75ac53bde2a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this notebook, we conduct a series of thought experiments on gravitation \
(Newtonian and Einsteinian) and electrostatics (classical and quantum). We \
begin with the question \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]what is the radius required \
for two identical balls separated by 1 meter to exert a static gravitational \
force of 1 Newton on each other.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] We find, by a \
Newtonian calculation, that they must weigh about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     SqrtBox["G"]}], "\[TildeTilde]", "122.4"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"bc923896-62b2-47c8-8bb7-ca695accd872"],
 " metric tonnes, and slightly less by General Relativity. \n\nWe evaluate \
these requirements across six  material densities, spanning terrestrial \
metals (Osmium, Gold, Lead, Iron) and degenerate astrophysical matter (White \
Dwarf and Neutron Star cores). \n\nWe then evaluate the feasibility of \
balancing this gravitational attraction with an equal electrostatic \
repulsion. For terrestrial metal spheres, achieving this balance is \
mechanically viable but severely constrained by manufacturing, environmental \
toxicity, and security logistics, leaving cast steel (Iron) as the only \
practically executable candidate.\n\nConversely, for degenerate spheres, the \
extreme charge concentration required for electrostatic balance creates \
surface electric fields that far exceed the Fowler-Nordheim threshold, \
triggering instantaneous quantum field emission (vacuum discharge). \
Electrostatic pressure remains below the Coulomb explosion threshold for all \
materials. \n\nFinally, we model mutual polarization (charge redistribution) \
using the method of images, demonstrating that while ordinary metal spheres \
experience a  30% reduction in repulsive force due to \
polarization\[LongDash]demanding a large reduction in gap distance or an \
increase in  charge\[LongDash]degenerate spheres remain unaffected due to \
their sub-millimeter geometries."
}], "Abstract",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990109365328333*^9, 3.990109501694192*^9}, {
  3.99010959906285*^9, 3.9901097359654922`*^9}, {3.9901097676573668`*^9, 
  3.9901097680528316`*^9}, {3.990109900747385*^9, 3.9901099428451433`*^9}, {
  3.990110012702984*^9, 3.990110058559215*^9}, {3.990110337448719*^9, 
  3.990110353495122*^9}, {3.9901104411503487`*^9, 3.9901105229725447`*^9}, {
  3.990364659843298*^9, 3.990364779579659*^9}, {3.990365554316654*^9, 
  3.990365581130291*^9}, {3.9903667798841057`*^9, 3.990366866056381*^9}, {
  3.990366910225017*^9, 3.990366926574564*^9}, {3.9904016389981337`*^9, 
  3.990401652406631*^9}, {3.9907328352492456`*^9, 3.990732881050536*^9}, {
  3.990743905628756*^9, 3.990743907135666*^9}, {3.990744087681891*^9, 
  3.9907440888164377`*^9}, {3.990744122678672*^9, 3.990744322971353*^9}, {
  3.990792597977955*^9, 
  3.990792608802737*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ddb79dbc-3e42-4c5f-a193-\
1dbb01f81462"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Radius at Density for 1 Newton Grav Force", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990367666990205*^9, 3.990367692909614*^9}, {
  3.990374640583378*^9, 
  3.990374648062855*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0e28a27e-bdc3-4c37-990d-\
642e8389d130"],

Cell["\<\
Ask \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]given a density \[Rho] of matter, what are the \
radii required of two identical balls to produce a \
1\[NoBreak]-\[NoBreak]Newton gravitational force (about \
3.6\[NonBreakingSpace]ounces of force) at a surface-to-surface separation of \
one meter?\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990374442904737*^9, 3.99037447186042*^9}, {
  3.990374542845318*^9, 3.990374629736451*^9}, {3.990398091556761*^9, 
  3.990398095316925*^9}, {3.990398317109047*^9, 3.990398330993519*^9}, {
  3.99040033902289*^9, 3.990400410297991*^9}, {3.990405836544868*^9, 
  3.990405867574214*^9}, {3.990732954298958*^9, 
  3.990732955907049*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"128c13b3-f4d2-4d44-8b94-\
06491e8f92a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The center-to-center distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["d", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "c17a6d88-8d06-49f4-9975-a509ed599f73"],
 " between the two balls is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    RowBox[{"2", "R"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "8068d1d0-8faa-42d4-93d3-c0b481a87a58"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["R", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "96575c7c-27a1-4ef7-96a9-f551cb633c05"],
 " is the radius of a ball. The mass of a ball is its density times its \
volume:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9903982879219627`*^9, 3.990398306885373*^9}, {
  3.990398341836647*^9, 3.99039836104135*^9}, {3.990398400645627*^9, 
  3.9903984200139303`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7273ea96-2101-48dd-9daa-\
e35b53e97d9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"m", "=", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]"}], "3"], 
    SuperscriptBox["R", "3"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9903984245523663`*^9, 
  3.9903984810981073`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"07fcc6d4-3281-4cbe-a405-\
72ba81c2e42f"],

Cell["One Newton of Newtonian gravitational force is", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990398532360455*^9, 
  3.990398563055167*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74f2118f-edb3-4b4d-8480-\
2da807336883"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"1", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"G", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], 
      SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"G", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]"}], "3"], 
         SuperscriptBox["R", "3"]}], 
        RowBox[{"1", "+", 
         RowBox[{"2", "R"}]}]], ")"}], "2"]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9903985674775248`*^9, 3.990398701484831*^9}, {
  3.9903987943863907`*^9, 
  3.990398797288875*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d44dcc78-4258-4126-8217-\
4fe3c4ff403c"],

Cell["or", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990399995082596*^9, 
  3.990399995161178*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"43bffd67-08f2-4af8-b1c8-\
c4f267581e7f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["3", 
    RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]", " ", "\[Rho]", 
     SqrtBox["G"]}]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", "3"], 
    RowBox[{"1", "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", "R"}]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9903996668806057`*^9, 3.9903998741164083`*^9}, {
  3.990399908331437*^9, 3.9903999083332157`*^9}, {3.990400043220379*^9, 
  3.99040005702464*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7a1d04ba-457d-462c-b035-\
48263dd5c533"],

Cell["Code this in Wolfram.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99073298565886*^9, 
  3.990732990296361*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5f90f63d-83c0-438f-9965-\
a250912205e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
  RowBox[{"G", ",", "R", ",", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990399928835096*^9, 3.990399931750557*^9}, {
  3.990399974409973*^9, 3.990399983639727*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"da6f312b-27b7-42fc-abb9-2ffad2f484c7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"G", "=", "6.67430*^-11"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"forceEqn", "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["3", 
       RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]", " ", "\[Rho]", 
        SqrtBox["G"]}]], "==", 
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox["R", "3"], 
       RowBox[{"1", "+", 
        RowBox[{"2", "R"}]}]]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99039994120848*^9, 3.990399969011627*^9}, {
  3.9904000671107893`*^9, 3.990400076628949*^9}, {3.990400119643796*^9, 
  3.990400154148851*^9}, {3.990733194447728*^9, 3.990733232384007*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8147607a-879c-456c-93a3-d41527b7a69b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  FractionBox["29221.90529157484`", "\[Rho]"], "\[Equal]", 
  FractionBox[
   SuperscriptBox["R", "3"], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "R"}]}]]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.990400079219993*^9, 3.990400157501712*^9, 
  3.990747777906363*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[2]=",ExpressionUUID->"1013ed9c-e04c-4488-95f6-2bd01a9960bf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Looking at three densities, that of Osmium at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["22.6", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "eceada27-eada-473f-a154-140bc3541f26"],
 " metric tonnes per cubic meter, of white-dwarf (electron-degenerate) matter \
at 29.3 million metric tonnes per cubic meter, and at neutron-star \
(nuclear-degenerate) matter at 400 trillion metric tonnes per cubic meter, we \
find radii within the normal range of human experience! "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990405140633559*^9, 3.990405290413542*^9}, {
   3.990405324141694*^9, 3.990405325504591*^9}, {3.990405362113056*^9, 
