  3.9907399874221163`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74bf214c-c8fc-459c-be83-\
27ab35f7c249"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Of course, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not remotely imaginable to have small \
balls of white-dwarf or neutron-star matter, even though their radii\
\[LongDash]1\[NonBreakingSpace]cm and \
41\[NonBreakingSpace]\[Mu]m\[LongDash]are easy to imagine. It turns out that \
it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s not ",
 StyleBox["practical",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to have balls of Osmium, Gold, or Lead, either. But it ",
 StyleBox["is",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " practical to do this experiment with balls of Iron if \
you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re willing to put up about $759\[NonBreakingSpace]M. We \
explain."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990406199770432*^9, 3.9904062898215313`*^9}, {
  3.990406379681868*^9, 3.990406386534196*^9}, {3.990406621834652*^9, 
  3.9904067455621347`*^9}, {3.990406781631337*^9, 3.990407097294066*^9}, {
  3.99073382618218*^9, 3.990733915221044*^9}, {3.990734328577876*^9, 
  3.990734365014656*^9}, {3.9907347740347977`*^9, 3.990734774677437*^9}, {
  3.99073924774166*^9, 
  3.9907392728549643`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2c44670b-76a0-4087-9607-\
55338c376a5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Osmium is rare",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the total annual production is about 1\[NonBreakingSpace]metric tonne per \
year, mostly as a by-product of Platinum mining, at a market price of about \
$13\[NonBreakingSpace]M\[NonBreakingSpace]/\[NonBreakingSpace]tonne The balls \
would consume the entire world output for 1130 years and cost about $14.5\
\[NonBreakingSpace]B. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990406199770432*^9, 3.9904062898215313`*^9}, {
  3.990406379681868*^9, 3.990406386534196*^9}, {3.990406621834652*^9, 
  3.9904067455621347`*^9}, {3.990406781631337*^9, 3.990407081149911*^9}, {
  3.990407334857288*^9, 3.9904073377018623`*^9}, {3.990408151727232*^9, 
  3.990408430140114*^9}, {3.990733933683117*^9, 3.990733963304288*^9}, {
  3.990734394719042*^9, 3.9907344147752857`*^9}, {3.990739295173964*^9, 
  3.990739319502158*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5cc48599-f8e3-4630-8310-\
b01929604488"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Osmium metallurgy is difficult",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": Osmium has a high melting point (3033\[NonBreakingSpace]\[Degree]C, or \
5491\[NonBreakingSpace]\[Degree]F) and is hard and brittle. It cannot be cast \
in a foundry, nor easily machined. To form large structures of Osmium, such \
as a 567\[NoBreak]-\[NoBreak]tonne sphere, powder-sintering metallurgy and \
hot isostatic pressing (HIP) are required. A specialized, vacuum-sealed \
furnace the size of a multi-story building at a cost of a couple of billion \
dollars, filled with osmium powder at staggering pressures and near-melting \
temperatures will be required to sinter the powder into a solid mass. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990406199770432*^9, 3.9904062898215313`*^9}, {
  3.990406379681868*^9, 3.990406386534196*^9}, {3.990406621834652*^9, 
  3.9904067455621347`*^9}, {3.990406781631337*^9, 3.990407081149911*^9}, {
  3.990407334857288*^9, 3.9904073377018623`*^9}, {3.990408151727232*^9, 
  3.990408430140114*^9}, {3.990733933683117*^9, 3.990734014250917*^9}, {
  3.9907340678426933`*^9, 3.990734124499612*^9}, {3.990739327655108*^9, 
  3.9907393282410183`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3f78958a-3fa8-401e-8562-\
15a12a92fe56"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Osmium is toxic",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": When heated near even trace amounts of oxygen, powdered osmium oxidizes \
into osmium tetroxide, a volatile, toxic liquid and gas that smells like \
chlorine. Even at microscopic concentrations in the air, it causes severe \
lung damage, permanent blindness by staining the cornea, and death. The \
environmental containment shielding required for a large-scale Osmium \
refinery alone would cost hundreds of millions of dollars. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990406199770432*^9, 3.9904062898215313`*^9}, {
   3.990406379681868*^9, 3.990406386534196*^9}, {3.990406621834652*^9, 
   3.9904067455621347`*^9}, {3.990406781631337*^9, 3.990407081149911*^9}, {
   3.990407334857288*^9, 3.9904073377018623`*^9}, {3.990408151727232*^9, 
   3.990408430140114*^9}, {3.990733933683117*^9, 3.990734014250917*^9}, {
   3.9907340678426933`*^9, 3.990734132304372*^9}, 3.99073444527781*^9, {
   3.990734597244463*^9, 
   3.990734647768907*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e22f9055-9308-4ad4-a4fc-\
a66c73af2491"],

Cell["\<\
The entire Osmium project would cost on the order of $20\[NonBreakingSpace]B, \
including transport (see below), about twice the capital expenditure cost of \
the James Webb Space Telescope or four times cost of the Large Hadron \
Collider.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9904084372986803`*^9, 3.990408485627761*^9}, {
  3.990734470104356*^9, 3.990734478325901*^9}, {3.99073453342671*^9, 
  3.9907345726272717`*^9}, {3.990734666517456*^9, 3.990734668097608*^9}, {
  3.9907398281450863`*^9, 
  3.990739830306547*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"724d7693-ab81-4f01-a219-\
d71310fa893d"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["We note, in passing, that Osmium has many commercial \
uses in small amounts. As a trivium, before the era of sapphire and diamond \
phonograph needles, slippery Osmium alloys were common in phonographs because \
they were relatively heavy and non-wearing on vinyl grooves of phongraph \
records.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990739845194018*^9, 
  3.9907399599116163`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf0f0c4a-5690-46f1-a0df-\
1382c144718b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Gold, Lead, Iron", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990739999854329*^9, 
  3.9907400061883802`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"56dfab3d-6418-475d-badd-\
c4dcd5274575"],

Cell["\<\
On the other hand, realizing the thought experiment with the required 1600-\
\[NoBreak]tonne\[NonBreakingSpace]balls of Iron of the required 10\[NoBreak]-\
\[NoBreak]foot radius would not so upset the geopolitical and environmental \
equilibria. Projects of this scale are the daily business of shipbuilders. \
The entire project could be effected for around $750\[NonBreakingSpace]M. \
With gold, the project would cost about $91\[NonBreakingSpace]B, mostly in \
material value and security, and with lead, about $590\[NonBreakingSpace]M. \
Gold and Lead would require significant civil engineering to counteract \
sagging and fracture of the huge balls, however. Iron would be, by far, the \
easiest material with which to realize our thought experiments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9904084879899063`*^9, 3.990408722444524*^9}, {
  3.9904087689652452`*^9, 3.990409028835074*^9}, {3.990734692809114*^9, 
  3.9907347228731527`*^9}, {3.990734785589582*^9, 
  3.9907348175622377`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e452d07e-72d2-47fb-9af0-\
0cdd5dad0ea2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Current approximate raw material prices per kg (as of mid-2026)\n",
  
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.98, 0.56, 0.17]],
 "Osmium: ~$12,860/kg\nGold: ~$75,000/kg (approx \
$2300-2400/oz\[LongDash]highly variable)\nLead: ~$2.10/kg\nIron (industrial \
scrap/refined steel scale): ~$0.40/kg"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990734853454862*^9, 3.9907348583257513`*^9}, 
   3.9907354219199953`*^9, {3.990736259006373*^9, 3.9907362736986027`*^9}, {
   3.9907363202500353`*^9, 3.990736365900879*^9}, {3.9907364034472437`*^9, 
   3.99073645931765*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1040f99b-8ddd-4dca-975c-\
0b2a87227503"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Annual global production in metric tonnes\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.98, 0.56, 0.17]],
 "Osmium: 1\nGold: 3600\nLead: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4500000", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bac26f3e-ea55-4e67-87c3-60ca6cf79d15"],
 "\nIron: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2500", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", "6"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "21e386e7-4e3f-49d0-8cf0-12e16dad5247"],
 " (Iron ore/pig iron)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990734853454862*^9, 3.9907348583257513`*^9}, 
   3.9907354219199953`*^9, {3.990736259006373*^9, 3.9907362736986027`*^9}, {
   3.9907363202500353`*^9, 3.990736365900879*^9}, 3.9907364034472437`*^9, {
   3.9907364639559517`*^9, 
   3.990736599780876*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"47e6fff1-2761-4497-9c88-\
810026a549c3"],

Cell["\<\
As the density of the material drops, the physical size of the spheres must \
grow to compensate. This growth pushes the centers of mass further apart, \
demanding a significantly higher total tonnage to achieve 1\[NoBreak]-\
\[NoBreak]Newton attractive force. However, because Gold, Lead, and Iron are \
vastly more common than Osmium, we cross the threshold from \
macro-geopolitical impossibility into mere heavy civil engineering.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990734853454862*^9, 3.9907348583257513`*^9}, 
   3.9907354219199953`*^9, {3.990736259006373*^9, 3.9907362736986027`*^9}, {
   3.9907363202500353`*^9, 3.990736365900879*^9}, 3.9907364034472437`*^9, {
   3.9907364639559517`*^9, 
   3.990736727190815*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"71c23ef9-3129-4fa1-9b4a-\
56bea76cc699"],

