Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Balancing Gravitation with Electrostatics", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990405955987832*^9, 
  3.9904059656833353`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"45429fc7-3896-4494-a761-\
f83a7f70402f"],

Cell["\<\
Now imagine accumulating a sufficient number of electrons on the surfaces of \
the balls to effect an electrostatic repulsive force of one Newton, \
counteracting the gravitational force. There are two immediate concerns with \
even the simplest assumptions: discharge via quantum tunneling (Field \
Emission, spontaneous vacuum discharge via quantum tunneling) and Coulomb \
Explosion (charge-induced structural rupture). \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9904059834341917`*^9, 3.990406010577263*^9}, {
  3.9907380007196198`*^9, 3.99073804441208*^9}, {3.990740152749503*^9, 
  3.990740168836887*^9}, {3.990740562143485*^9, 3.990740563146804*^9}, {
  3.990740625582654*^9, 3.990740693745644*^9}, {3.990740845356642*^9, 
  3.990740892452668*^9}, {3.990741709582397*^9, 
  3.990741711105256*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"49288871-0c05-4d64-a72f-\
0c42e82fcc43"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Degenerate Discharge", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99074171840021*^9, 
  3.990741722798723*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0b428e32-5805-4756-a54c-\
124a9ab9a5fe"],

Cell["\<\
For white-dwarf and neutron-star spheres, the electric field reaches extreme \
levels (9.56 \[Times] 10\:2078  V/m and 5.43 \[Times] 10\.b9\.b3  V/m), \
resulting in instantaneous field emission discharge.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990741739998785*^9, 
  3.990741761735124*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6a50ed92-e13a-40bc-953b-\
23e3b7f21c12"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Coulomb Explosion", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990741802398301*^9, 
  3.990741807293681*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7d3258f8-84b3-49bc-86ac-\
0b08ec906b51"],

Cell["While electrostatic tension", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990741813271446*^9, 
  3.9907418208804502`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fb0100ad-7c12-445d-87e8-\
8ca0e5bceffe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"P", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "0"], 
    SuperscriptBox["E", "2"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9907418334521914`*^9, 
  3.990741864094479*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b9a21468-6c3a-48b6-bb0f-\
1d93df1776d0"],

Cell["\<\
is huge for the neutron-star sphere (\[TildeTilde]1.3 \[Times] 10\.b9\:2076  \
Pa), it is still many orders of magnitude below the astronomical bulk modulus \
of nuclear matter (\[TildeTilde]10\.b3\.b3  Pa). Therefore, none of the \
spheres in the 1-Newton configuration explode.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990741813271446*^9, {3.990741870751334*^9, 
   3.990741892207906*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7634a3cb-c88c-4aa8-a3a4-\
823b2d7b1e8a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Computations", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9907419007879543`*^9, 
  3.9907419022310257`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f7ab9cf8-0986-497c-bbc0-\
860225a357bc"],

Cell["\<\
The following Wolfram code computes charges, electron counts, electrostatic \
pressure, and risks for Field Emission and Coulomb Explosion via textbook \
formulae:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990740963964057*^9, 3.990740980566533*^9}, {
  3.990741359630117*^9, 3.990741421854061*^9}, {3.990741522595544*^9, 
  3.99074152840971*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"915b84f3-0a34-423c-b3e7-\
ab4fe300bb7c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", "Constants", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"G", "=", "6.67430*^-11"}], ";"}], "           ", 
   RowBox[{"(*", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"m", "^", "3"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"kg", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"s", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}]}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ke", "=", "8.98755*^9"}], ";"}], "             ", 
   RowBox[{"(*", 
    RowBox[{"N", " ", 
     RowBox[{"m", "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"C", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}]}], "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"eps0", "=", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]", " ", "ke"}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "         ", 
   RowBox[{"(*", 
    RowBox[{"F", "/", "m"}], "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"eElem", "=", "1.602176634*^-19"}], ";"}], " ", 
